WEBVTT

00:00.780 --> 00:03.770
<i>As Otomo Middle School was one goal behind Nankatsu,</i>

00:03.770 --> 00:09.780
<i>Nitta imitates Tsubasa's Non-Trap Running Volley Shot, showing rapid improvement.</i>

00:09.780 --> 00:15.200
<i>At the same time, Nankatsu's attacks are all stymied by Urabe, the team and the goalkeeper, Ichijo.</i>

00:15.200 --> 00:20.250
<i>With the long pass that Nitta received from their goal, he managed to finally complete his special move.</i>

00:20.250 --> 00:25.460
Go! Non-Trap Running Volley Falcon Shot for you!

00:25.460 --> 00:28.380
<i>Otomo Middle School finally catch up to Nankatsu.</i>

00:28.380 --> 00:32.000
<i>However, Tsubasa isn't planning to sit down and watch that continue.</i>

00:34.440 --> 00:40.900
<i>He returns the goal right back against them, and Nankatsu are back in the lead again with a score of 2-1.</i>

00:41.810 --> 00:45.600
<i>Nankatsu Middle School scores another goal thanks to Tsubasa's splendid shot.</i>

00:45.600 --> 00:47.260
<i>If they score on you, you score back!</i>

00:47.260 --> 00:50.110
<i>Things have taken a fierce turn.</i>

00:50.110 --> 00:56.320
<i>Furthermore, this goal was the fruit of Nankatsu's attackers' efforts in breaking through Otomo's defense,</i>

00:56.320 --> 00:59.330
<i>despite Tsubasa being kept under control all game.</i>

00:59.700 --> 01:02.280
<i>That's why it is all the more important.</i>

01:03.070 --> 01:06.210
<i>So, Nankatsu is motivated to win their 3rd championship...</i>

01:06.210 --> 01:10.680
<i>But... I have mastered the Non-Trap Falcon Shot!</i>

01:10.680 --> 01:13.240
<i>I'll show them we can overtake them right away!</i>

01:16.220 --> 01:18.930
<i>Ai! Ai! Ai!</i>

01:16.220 --> 01:18.930
<i>Love! Love! Love!</i>

01:19.850 --> 01:22.520
<i>Ai! Ai! Ai!</i>

01:19.850 --> 01:22.520
<i>Love! Love! Love!</i>

01:23.430 --> 01:26.140
<i>Ai! Ai! Ai!</i>

01:23.430 --> 01:26.140
<i>Love! Love! Love!</i>

01:33.030 --> 01:35.860
<i>moeru you ni hitori demo</i>

01:33.030 --> 01:35.860
<i>I keep running, lying to myself</i>

01:35.860 --> 01:42.120
<i>ikiteyukeru to usobuite hashiritsudzukete</i>

01:35.860 --> 01:42.120
<i>that I can live alone, though the loneliness makes me burn</i>

01:42.120 --> 01:48.000
<i>unubore no morosa wo kimi wa shitteta na no ni</i>

01:42.120 --> 01:48.000
<i>You knew how fragile my self-conceit makes me</i>

01:48.000 --> 01:54.590
<i>kokoro made uchinomaresareta kono yoru ni</i>

01:48.000 --> 01:54.590
<i>In this night that even shattered my heart</i>

01:54.590 --> 01:58.590
<i>kimi no koe sagasu</i>

01:54.590 --> 01:58.590
<i>I hate how weak I am</i>

01:58.590 --> 02:03.100
<i>kono yowasa ga nikui yo</i>

01:58.590 --> 02:03.100
<i>yearning for your voice</i>

02:03.100 --> 02:08.640
<i>ima sugu torimodoshi ni ikanakya</i>

02:03.100 --> 02:08.640
<i>"I've got to get you back right now!"</i>

02:08.640 --> 02:10.230
<i>baka darou?</i>

02:08.640 --> 02:10.230
<i>I'm stupid, right?</i>

02:10.230 --> 02:11.440
<i>ai</i>

02:10.230 --> 02:11.440
<i>Love!</i>

02:11.440 --> 02:14.940
<i>kizudarake no ai wo shinjite</i>

02:11.440 --> 02:14.940
<i>Believing in my scarred love</i>

02:14.940 --> 02:24.830
<i>nagareochita namida sae mo tsuyosa e to kaete</i>

02:14.940 --> 02:24.830
<i>I will turn these shedded tears into strength</i>

02:24.830 --> 02:25.660
<i>ai</i>

02:24.830 --> 02:25.660
<i>Love!</i>

02:25.660 --> 02:29.460
<i>kizudarake no ai da to shite mo</i>

02:25.660 --> 02:29.460
<i>Even though it is a scarred love</i>

02:29.460 --> 02:33.460
<i>bokura no sekai wo tomoshiteru</i>

02:29.460 --> 02:33.460
<i>it lightens up our world</i>

02:33.460 --> 02:39.720
<i>kono ai mo ichido taritomo</i>

02:33.460 --> 02:39.720
<i>I will not let go of this love</i>

02:39.720 --> 02:42.510
<i>hanasanai</i>

02:39.720 --> 02:42.510
<i>for a single moment!</i>

02:44.260 --> 02:48.520
<b><b>EPISODE 32:
OVERTHROW TSUBASA! HYUGA VS. MISUGI</b></b>

02:45.770 --> 02:48.770
<i>We are about to pass the 20-minute mark of the final match.</i>

02:50.140 --> 02:52.020
<i>The ball is sent to Taki on the wing.</i>

02:53.930 --> 02:55.530
<i>Urabe steals the ball!</i>

02:56.780 --> 02:57.740
Nitta!

02:57.740 --> 02:59.740
<i>Otomo attacks with a long pass!</i>

02:59.740 --> 03:01.740
<i>Will it reach Nitta?</i>

03:01.740 --> 03:02.490
All right!

03:03.710 --> 03:07.830
<i>No, Izawa jumps and intercepts it!</i>

03:07.830 --> 03:08.700
What?!

03:10.950 --> 03:13.650
<i>After Nitta mastered the Non-Trap Falcon Shot,</i>

03:13.650 --> 03:16.920
<i>everyone's focused on reading the course of the passes.</i>

03:16.920 --> 03:21.340
<i>From the start of the second half, Nankatsu's become used to Otomo's speed</i>

03:21.340 --> 03:24.550
<i>and has been keeping up with their pace.</i>

03:25.410 --> 03:26.060
Nitta!

03:26.520 --> 03:27.720
It's all yours, Takasugi!

03:27.720 --> 03:28.700
Yeah!

03:28.700 --> 03:30.140
<i>Another interception!</i>

03:30.140 --> 03:31.300
<i>Damn it!</i>

03:31.300 --> 03:35.110
<i>And here I am, certain to score, so long as I get the ball...</i>

03:35.110 --> 03:37.860
<i>We're about to reach the 23rd minute of the second half.</i>

03:38.800 --> 03:40.860
<i>Nishio steals the ball!</i>

03:45.580 --> 03:46.800
Nitta!

03:46.800 --> 03:49.440
<i>Otomo sends a long pass to the front.</i>

03:49.440 --> 03:50.080
Okay!

03:52.680 --> 03:55.520
<i>But Nitta is offside!</i>

03:55.520 --> 03:56.290
What?!

03:56.290 --> 03:58.000
<i>That was well done!</i>

03:58.000 --> 04:00.180
<i>Nankatsu's defenders see through Otomo</i>

04:00.180 --> 04:03.340
<i>and set an offside trap for them!</i>

04:03.340 --> 04:06.850
Damn it! Our passes are completely read!

04:06.850 --> 04:09.350
<i>A mere 5 minutes remain.</i>

04:10.520 --> 04:12.560
<i>This time, it's Nankatsu's turn to attack.</i>

04:12.960 --> 04:17.880
<i>We can't let Nitta's Non-Trap Falcon Shot go unused!</i>

04:18.840 --> 04:20.990
<i>However, Otomo's defense is fervent!</i>

04:21.390 --> 04:21.940
All right!

04:21.940 --> 04:22.560
What?!

04:22.560 --> 04:24.980
<i>Ishizaki picks up the rebound.</i>

04:24.980 --> 04:27.680
<i>Ishizaki overlaps and runs up the sideline.</i>

04:27.680 --> 04:28.280
Here!

04:28.280 --> 04:30.150
<i>It's a cross!</i>

04:30.150 --> 04:33.290
<i>But isn't it headed a little bit too far?</i>

04:33.800 --> 04:36.670
<i>It's not, Tsubasa's closing onto the point!</i>

04:36.670 --> 04:41.460
Ichijo! Tsubasa will shoot, even if there's no shooting angle!

04:41.460 --> 04:44.590
<i>Tsubasa fires a shot after trapping the ball for a second.</i>

04:45.200 --> 04:47.300
<i>However, it's off-target.</i>

04:47.300 --> 04:49.060
All right!

04:50.360 --> 04:52.810
<i>Taki plunges in with a diving header!</i>

04:53.580 --> 04:54.810
<i>It's the 3rd goal!</i>

04:54.810 --> 04:58.810
<i>Their goalkeeper Ichijo has been completely outplayed by Tsubasa.</i>

04:58.810 --> 05:03.780
<i>In this final stage, Nankatsu scores again at the end of the game as if they hit the nail to the coffin.</i>

05:03.780 --> 05:07.280
Damn it all! Is this Nankatsu's true face?

05:07.280 --> 05:10.360
<i>There's only added time left in the game.</i>

05:10.360 --> 05:13.160
<i>This victory is as good as Nankatsu's.</i>

05:13.160 --> 05:19.100
<i>He doesn't just score himself,
he also makes use of his teammates to score.</i>

05:19.100 --> 05:20.960
<i>So, this is Tsubasa Ozora...</i>

05:21.600 --> 05:24.380
<i>Despite that, I won't give up until the very end!</i>

05:26.500 --> 05:28.890
<i>Otomo continues to attack, refusing to give up!</i>

05:28.890 --> 05:32.890
<i>Our duty is to get the ball to Nitta until the very end.</i>

05:34.020 --> 05:35.480
<i>We'll get the ball to Nitta!</i>

05:36.160 --> 05:37.020
Urabe...

05:37.020 --> 05:38.900
<i>We'll get the ball to Nitta!</i>

05:39.400 --> 05:40.480
<i>It's what we must do!</i>

05:43.760 --> 05:47.040
<i>The whistle has blown!</i>

05:47.040 --> 05:49.100
<i>Nankatsu has won!</i>

05:49.100 --> 05:49.910
We won!

05:51.490 --> 05:54.620
God damn it!

05:59.270 --> 06:00.130
Nitta!

06:04.160 --> 06:09.000
<i>Nitta fired a perfect non-trap shot into the goal, but it's too little, too late.</i>

06:09.920 --> 06:13.640
<i>The winner of the National Middle School Football Tournament's</i>

06:13.640 --> 06:17.380
<i>Shizuoka Prefectural Tournament is Nankatsu,
for the third time in row.</i>

06:17.380 --> 06:18.330
We did it!

06:18.330 --> 06:20.780
We'll go to the National Tournament again!

06:21.980 --> 06:25.270
<i>Otomo Middle School held even with Nankatsu throughout the game,</i>

06:25.270 --> 06:28.240
<i>but their strength ran out before they could really put up a fight.</i>

06:28.240 --> 06:33.950
<i>Nankatsu won because they prevented Otomo from sending the ball to Nitta at the end. It shows their strength.</i>

06:33.950 --> 06:34.740
Yes.

06:35.340 --> 06:38.500
<i>All right! Now we will play against Nankatsu once more!</i>

06:41.500 --> 06:42.750
Received Messages

06:41.500 --> 06:42.750
From

06:41.500 --> 06:42.750
To

06:41.500 --> 06:42.750
Japanese National Football Federa...

06:41.500 --> 06:42.750
Munemasa Katagiri

06:41.500 --> 06:42.750
Business Contact

06:41.500 --> 06:42.750
I'm contacting you to inform you

06:41.500 --> 06:42.750
that Mr. Mikami has just landed

06:41.500 --> 06:42.750
in Narita Airport. Please come to

06:41.500 --> 06:42.750
the meeting that will be held at

06:41.500 --> 06:42.750
the Federation's office in Yoyogi.

06:45.280 --> 06:47.480
Nankatsu is really strong.

06:47.480 --> 06:50.660
It was worth the trip to come watch them.

06:50.660 --> 06:51.840
You're right.

06:53.500 --> 06:55.770
I'm sorry, Nitta.

06:56.780 --> 07:00.770
It's our fault for not being able to get the ball to you.

07:02.350 --> 07:05.270
It's not your fault.

07:05.270 --> 07:09.920
I have completely lost to Tsubasa Ozora in this match.

07:15.160 --> 07:16.540
<i>I have made up my mind.</i>

07:17.370 --> 07:23.040
<i>My goal from now on, Tsubasa, is to catch up to you and eventually surpass you.</i>

07:23.040 --> 07:28.100
Tsubasa, congratulations for your third consecutive victory in Shizuoka Prefectural Tournament.

07:28.100 --> 07:29.300
Thank you very much.

07:29.300 --> 07:35.320
You're once again headed to the Nationals. Do you already have a player you want to play against?

07:35.320 --> 07:37.560
Someone I want to play against?

07:38.750 --> 07:45.310
The player I want to play against the most right now is Taro Misaki!

07:45.310 --> 07:46.060
Misaki?

07:46.060 --> 07:47.150
Taro?

07:47.150 --> 07:48.360
What did he say?

07:48.360 --> 07:54.270
By Misaki, do you mean the Misaki you used to form a duo with in elementary school?

07:54.270 --> 07:55.370
Yes, the very one.

07:56.050 --> 08:00.540
Ever since the National Youth Football Tournament, he's not been heard of around the world of football.

08:00.540 --> 08:06.890
People have theorized that he's been unable to return due to his leg injury during that tournament.

08:06.890 --> 08:09.630
That's impossible. We're talking about Misaki, here!

08:11.090 --> 08:14.420
I'm sure he's still playing football somewhere.

08:16.190 --> 08:17.220
I'm sure of it.

08:18.750 --> 08:23.480
<i>Damn it! He wants to play against Misaki the most?</i>

08:23.480 --> 08:30.690
<i>Tsubasa, I'll make you remember once more that I, the almighty Kojiro Hyuga, am also in the National Tournament!</i>

08:31.120 --> 08:32.070
Let's do this!

08:32.070 --> 08:36.940
We'll smash Musashi Middle School tomorrow, and head to the Nationals as Tokyo's representatives!

08:36.940 --> 08:37.700
Yeah!

08:38.200 --> 08:42.670
<i>The champion of the Shizuoka Prefectural Tournament, Nankatsu Middle School.</i>

08:45.600 --> 08:46.960
Ishizaki!

08:47.420 --> 08:48.540
We have lost.

08:48.540 --> 08:51.210
I have made a promise. I await your orders.

08:51.210 --> 08:51.960
What?

08:52.610 --> 08:55.780
It's okay, Urabe. Let's just forget about that.

08:55.780 --> 08:58.590
I can't have that. I made a man's promise.

08:58.590 --> 09:02.000
Then cheer for us at the Nationals.

09:02.000 --> 09:02.770
That'll be enough.

09:02.770 --> 09:05.480
Are you sure that you don't want anything else?

09:05.480 --> 09:06.930
Yes.

09:06.930 --> 09:09.730
All right then! I'll be cheering a lot for you!

09:09.730 --> 09:11.850
In return, don't you dare lose.

09:11.850 --> 09:15.080
You are the representatives of our Shizuoka Prefecture.

09:15.080 --> 09:16.240
O-okay...

09:19.030 --> 09:19.600
JAPANESE NATIONAL FOOTBALL FEDERATION

09:19.950 --> 09:23.540
Congratulations on completing those
2,5 years of training, Mr. Mikami.

09:23.540 --> 09:26.420
Thanks, Katagiri.

09:26.420 --> 09:29.190
Forgive my abruptness, but here are the documents I spoke of.

09:29.190 --> 09:32.510
Oh, boy... I've barely set foot back in Japan, you know...

09:32.510 --> 09:38.580
Mr. Mikami, you'll be the coach of the national middle school selection team.

09:38.580 --> 09:41.660
We'd like you to handle this very important task.

09:40.010 --> 09:44.020
SIGN: MIDDLE SCHOOL FOOTBALL TOURNAMENT
CANDIDATE LIST FOR THE SELECTION

09:41.720 --> 09:44.020
So I won't have any time to rest, I take it?

09:44.520 --> 09:46.820
How is Wakabayashi doing?

09:46.820 --> 09:48.770
He's working hard, as usual.

09:49.180 --> 09:55.150
Surrounded by high-level professional players in Germany, his skills are quickly developing.

09:56.140 --> 10:00.370
Even though I'm not there for him, he can do well enough by himself.

10:00.370 --> 10:03.370
It looks like Tsubasa's grown a lot too.

10:03.370 --> 10:05.270
Yes, of course.

10:05.270 --> 10:09.380
I'd dare say that there's no player in Japan who could be called his equal.

10:09.380 --> 10:14.670
Will Tsubasa rise to legend by accomplishing a third National championship,

10:14.670 --> 10:17.130
or will his rivals stop him in his quest?

10:17.820 --> 10:23.140
Tsubasa and his friends' last summer is quickly approaching.

10:18.300 --> 10:22.640
HOKKAIDO FINALS
FURANO MIDDLE SCHOOL - SATSUNISHI MIDDLE SCHOOL

10:25.600 --> 10:28.100
<i>The whirlwind of Furano is raging in Hokkaido.</i>

10:25.680 --> 10:28.770
FURANO MIDDLE SCHOOL CAPTAIN
HIKARU MATSUYAMA

10:28.100 --> 10:28.760
Here!

10:30.650 --> 10:34.650
All right, go! We'll score as many goals as we can!

10:34.650 --> 10:36.370
Yes, captain!

10:36.370 --> 10:39.060
<i>This is how Furano plays with all of their members.</i>

10:39.060 --> 10:41.870
<i>Their teamwork is second to none in Japan.</i>

10:41.870 --> 10:43.870
Go! Shoot!

10:46.060 --> 10:48.700
<i>The match ends! 7-0!</i>

10:48.700 --> 10:50.520
<i>Furano Middle School wins!</i>

10:51.880 --> 10:54.710
<i>They want to take this Furano whirlwind to Nationals,</i>

10:54.710 --> 10:58.670
<i>and return to Hokkaido this year with the championship pennant.</i>

10:58.670 --> 11:01.470
Just wait for us, Nankatsu...! Tsubasa!

11:01.850 --> 11:05.850
AKITA PREFECTURE FINAL
HANAWA MIDDLE SCHOOL - SAKURADA MIDDLE SCHOOL

11:02.340 --> 11:07.850
<i>We're in the Akita Prefectural Tournament finals!
Hanawa's Tachibana Twins' miraculous football takes flight!</i>

11:08.500 --> 11:09.730
It's them again!

11:10.650 --> 11:16.730
<i>With their ever-changing attacks, these two have scored 90% of Hanawa's goals.</i>

11:16.730 --> 11:18.280
Let's do this, Kazuo!

11:18.280 --> 11:19.360
Yeah, Masao!

11:21.620 --> 11:22.360
<i>Goal!</i>

11:22.360 --> 11:24.340
<i>It's the 5th goal of the match.</i>

11:25.110 --> 11:28.950
We'll be the national champion this year.

11:29.290 --> 11:31.440
<i>We're in added time of the second half!</i>

11:29.330 --> 11:32.920
OSAKA PREFECTURE FINAL
NANIWA MIDDLE SCHOOL - AZUMAICHI MIDDLE SCHOOL

11:31.440 --> 11:32.920
<i>Naniwa is struggling!</i>

11:33.210 --> 11:36.700
<i>Even though they've kept the score at 0-0 thanks to Nakanishi's efforts,</i>

11:33.710 --> 11:37.880
NANIWA MIDDLE SCHOOL
TAICHI NAKANISHI

11:36.700 --> 11:38.530
<i>they can't seem to score a goal!</i>

11:38.530 --> 11:41.340
<i>Please, just one goal! Just score one goal!</i>

11:41.940 --> 11:45.430
<i>Azumaichi's defender Soda steals the ball!</i>

11:45.430 --> 11:48.140
<i>I will be going to the Nationals!</i>

11:49.770 --> 11:54.360
Let's go, Nakanishi, have a taste of my Razor Shot!

11:54.360 --> 11:57.480
<i>Soda fires off a long shot with all he's got!</i>

11:57.480 --> 11:59.320
I won't let you score!

12:00.480 --> 12:01.360
What?!

12:02.840 --> 12:04.110
All right!

12:04.910 --> 12:06.490
<i>Naniwa is defeated!</i>

12:06.490 --> 12:10.800
<i>Azumaichi Middle School earns a ticket to the Nationals for the first time.</i>

12:10.800 --> 12:13.040
This can't be happening...

12:13.040 --> 12:15.040
— TOKYO —

12:15.940 --> 12:19.890
<i>Can you hear all those cheers?</i>

12:19.890 --> 12:26.140
<i>After his 2-years long rehab, the Young Noble of the Field, Jun Misugi is back in the game again!</i>

12:34.020 --> 12:38.780
<i>Since the National Youth Football Tournament, The "Ace of Glass" Jun Misugi,</i>

12:38.780 --> 12:42.580
<i>still battling his heart disease, finally makes his return to the spotlight</i>

12:39.400 --> 12:44.070
MUSASHI MIDDLE SCHOOL CAPTAIN
JUN MISUGI

12:42.580 --> 12:46.740
<i>in this 3rd year of middle school after enduring a tough rehabilitation process!</i>

12:47.610 --> 12:51.750
<i>I've returned to the pitch once more.</i>

12:51.750 --> 12:56.840
<i>As his personal doctor forbids him from heavy exercise lasting more than 30 minutes,</i>

12:56.840 --> 12:58.500
<i>he won't be able to play full-time.</i>

12:58.500 --> 13:06.270
<i>With his addition to Musashi's squad, they've made a beeline straight to the finals of this fierce tournament.</i>

13:06.270 --> 13:10.310
He is playing this well, even after taking a two year break. What an amazing boy.

13:11.100 --> 13:13.510
— 1 MONTH AGO —

13:11.620 --> 13:13.310
<i>Okay, that's fine.</i>

13:13.770 --> 13:15.980
<i>Is that true?</i>

13:15.980 --> 13:20.600
<i>So you are telling me that I can play football again, right?</i>

13:20.600 --> 13:24.510
<i>I just can't refuse your strong will and effort towards football.</i>

13:24.510 --> 13:26.570
<i>I will give you the permit for the tournament.</i>

13:27.350 --> 13:28.310
<i>That's it!</i>

13:28.310 --> 13:29.320
<i>I finally did it!</i>

13:29.320 --> 13:31.910
<i>Congratulations, Captain.</i>

13:31.910 --> 13:33.660
<i>Manager!</i>

13:33.660 --> 13:38.480
<i>Thank you for looking after me these past 2 years in so many different ways.</i>

13:38.480 --> 13:41.170
<i>It's thanks to you that I am able to play again.</i>

13:43.920 --> 13:44.970
<i>Sorry.</i>

13:44.970 --> 13:46.670
<i>Don't mention it.</i>

13:47.950 --> 13:49.930
<i>Being young is sure a bliss.</i>

13:50.640 --> 13:52.970
Do your best, Captain.

13:54.140 --> 13:56.730
SIGN: TOHO ACADEMY - WAITING ROOM

13:55.120 --> 13:56.730
As you may get from the data here,

13:56.730 --> 13:59.310
Musashi defends in the first half before shifting,

13:59.310 --> 14:02.230
betting it all in the second half when Misugi enters the game.

14:02.230 --> 14:04.940
Listen to me,

14:04.030 --> 14:07.240
TOHO ACADEMY COACH
MAKOTO KITAZUME

14:04.940 --> 14:09.180
We will score freely in the first half while Misugi is out, and finish them before he enters.

14:09.180 --> 14:10.240
Yes, sir!

14:10.980 --> 14:13.740
We gotta watch this final game properly, y'know.

14:13.740 --> 14:16.620
Nankatsu is not our only opponent.

14:16.620 --> 14:17.450
Indeed.

14:17.450 --> 14:20.460
<i>Both teams make their appearance.</i>

14:23.820 --> 14:30.130
<i>Toho Academy, aiming for their 3rd appearance in the National Tournament, puts their ace Hyuga as a starter</i>

14:30.130 --> 14:32.550
<i>despite mostly letting him rest until now.</i>

14:32.550 --> 14:38.810
<i>Musashi is not sending Misugi out there yet, opening the match with a defensive formation.</i>

14:39.420 --> 14:40.770
Hey, Sanae.

14:40.770 --> 14:43.570
Did I set it to record properly?

14:47.660 --> 14:49.030
Okay, that's it!

14:49.030 --> 14:51.320
Is it over already?

14:51.320 --> 14:53.260
It's because we just played yesterday.

14:53.260 --> 14:56.210
You should let your body rest and cool down for today.

14:56.210 --> 14:57.090
Yes, sir!

14:57.090 --> 15:00.670
All right, now I can have a look at Tokyo Tournament.

15:04.090 --> 15:07.420
We've got someone who doesn't know the meaning of rest over here.

15:07.420 --> 15:11.190
Tsubasa! The Tokyo Tournament finals are about to start.

15:11.190 --> 15:12.850
Give me a few more minutes.

15:17.400 --> 15:18.350
It's no good.

15:19.330 --> 15:22.440
<i>"Fire your long shots with a drive effect on them."</i>

15:22.440 --> 15:26.690
<i>"Unless you master that shot, you won't be able to become a first-class player," was it?</i>

15:27.610 --> 15:33.570
<i>Usually you shoot the ball with your body weight on it so it won't fly too high.</i>

15:33.570 --> 15:36.740
<i>The next level for this is the Drive Shot.</i>

15:37.440 --> 15:43.750
<i>This shot takes a sharp dive after flying in from up high, getting over the keeper and stealing a score.</i>

15:44.320 --> 15:46.750
<i>Roberto, this one is tough to master.</i>

15:47.780 --> 15:50.660
<i>Shots with spins added from the sides are easy</i>

15:50.660 --> 15:54.800
<i>but how do I add a forward spin —a drive— to a ball?</i>

15:55.810 --> 16:00.300
<i>If you were here to show me the basics, I might be able to figure it out quickly.</i>

16:00.300 --> 16:02.640
<i>I guess I'll just have to practice it by myself.</i>

16:03.990 --> 16:06.420
<i>Roberto, it's just one more year.</i>

16:06.420 --> 16:08.300
<i>I will be going to Brazil then.</i>

16:09.870 --> 16:15.050
Damn it, we can't let him train alone!

16:15.050 --> 16:17.030
Okay guys, we'll practice, too!

16:17.030 --> 16:17.800
All right!

16:17.800 --> 16:18.760
Tsubasa!

16:18.760 --> 16:20.660
We will accompany you too.

16:20.660 --> 16:25.510
<i>Sanae, how are the things going between you and Tsubasa after that?</i>

16:25.510 --> 16:27.380
<i>Is everything going well?</i>

16:27.380 --> 16:30.880
<i>Our relationship is so-so as you can see.</i>

16:35.860 --> 16:38.930
<i>Yayoi, it's impossible for us.</i>

16:38.930 --> 16:42.940
<i>All Tsubasa has his eyes on is football.</i>

16:45.880 --> 16:47.980
<i>Toho and Musashi...</i>

16:47.980 --> 16:49.980
<i>It's a fight between Hyuga and Misugi, huh?</i>

16:49.980 --> 16:54.240
<i>No matter which side wins, the winner will ultimately be me!</i>

16:54.240 --> 16:55.580
<i>Go!</i>

16:55.580 --> 16:59.490
<i>Sawada cuts through Musashi's intense defense by himself with a dribble.</i>

16:59.490 --> 17:01.040
Good going, Takeshi.

17:06.730 --> 17:08.210
<i>It's the third goal!</i>

17:08.210 --> 17:08.640
Hah!

17:08.640 --> 17:11.130
<i>He's scored a hat-trick in the first half already!</i>

17:11.130 --> 17:14.880
<i>Kojiro Hyuga is indeed the reigning ace striker in the whole country.</i>

17:15.360 --> 17:18.140
<i>Toho is incredibly strong with him on the team.</i>

17:18.140 --> 17:21.110
<i>On the other side, Musashi takes an exceptionally hurtful blow</i>

17:21.110 --> 17:22.930
<i>conceding this many in their defensive first half.</i>

17:23.720 --> 17:25.710
Coach, I will play.

17:25.710 --> 17:27.940
But Misugi, you're supposed to play the second half.

17:28.350 --> 17:31.680
If we concede any more goals, we will not be able to win this.

17:31.680 --> 17:33.520
I'll leave once 30 minutes pass.

17:33.520 --> 17:34.950
Let me play, Coach.

17:36.110 --> 17:39.030
<i>Musashi decides to make a substitution here.</i>

17:39.030 --> 17:41.370
consecutive "oh"

17:42.230 --> 17:43.750
<i>It's 20 minutes into the first half.</i>

17:43.750 --> 17:46.330
<i>Misugi comes on into the game!</i>

17:46.330 --> 17:49.710
<i>It's a drastic strategy, with the thought that they cannot take more goals.</i>

17:49.710 --> 17:51.700
<i>It's no use, Misugi.</i>

17:51.700 --> 17:56.220
<i>Even if you appear now, there is no way you guys can win over our Toho Academy.</i>

17:56.970 --> 17:59.500
Sorry, we let them score three times.

17:59.500 --> 18:00.600
What are you saying?

18:00.600 --> 18:02.460
It's just three goals.

18:02.460 --> 18:05.100
10 minutes left this half, 30 more left in the second half.

18:05.100 --> 18:08.230
If we score once every 10 minutes, we can win.

18:08.230 --> 18:10.150
Look, it starts now!

18:10.150 --> 18:13.740
Let's give them a taste of what Musashi's football is really like!

18:13.740 --> 18:14.740
Yes!

18:14.740 --> 18:18.840
<i>Musashi switches to offense as soon as Misugi comes on.</i>

18:18.840 --> 18:20.160
<i>The match resumes!</i>

18:23.200 --> 18:27.930
<i>Musashi entrusts the ball to their control tower, counting on him as a playmaker.</i>

18:28.760 --> 18:32.670
<i>Will Toho's overwhelming pace in this match be reversed?</i>

18:32.670 --> 18:34.090
Let's go Misugi.

18:34.090 --> 18:35.800
Take it as a greeting from us!

18:37.860 --> 18:38.550
What?!

18:38.550 --> 18:40.210
Go for it, Takeshi!

18:41.380 --> 18:42.180
Sawada!

18:43.430 --> 18:44.430
Got you!

18:45.680 --> 18:46.430
What?!

18:47.500 --> 18:50.940
<i>Even though he was off-guard, Misugi makes an elegant jump!</i>

18:51.940 --> 18:53.940
Let's go! We will have our first goal now!

18:53.940 --> 18:54.690
Okay!

18:54.690 --> 18:58.180
<i>Musashi's trio of forwards advances towards the goal.</i>

18:58.180 --> 19:00.700
<i>What kind of pass he will make, and to whom?</i>

19:00.700 --> 19:02.990
Mark them man-to-man!

19:02.990 --> 19:05.650
<i>Toho's defenders mark the trio.</i>

19:05.650 --> 19:12.250
<i>The one protecting the goal is the #1 middle school goalkeeper who hasn't conceded a goal this tournament, Wakashimazu!</i>

19:12.250 --> 19:13.910
<i>Here I come, Toho.</i>

19:13.910 --> 19:17.980
<i>I sacrificed these two years and bet everything on this 3rd year.</i>

19:17.980 --> 19:21.010
<i>Do you really think that I'd let myself lose here,</i>

19:21.010 --> 19:24.010
<i>before going to Nationals? Before meeting Tsubasa?</i>

19:25.260 --> 19:26.140
What?!

19:26.140 --> 19:27.980
<i>This is unexpected!</i>

19:27.980 --> 19:32.400
<i>He dribbles past the defense and makes his way to the goal, keeping the ball!</i>

19:32.400 --> 19:34.150
Crap, he outwitted us!

19:37.890 --> 19:40.480
<i>It's in! 3-1!</i>

19:40.480 --> 19:42.620
<i>Musashi scores first on their counter attack,</i>

19:42.620 --> 19:46.490
<i>just 1 minute and 30 seconds after Misugi joins the match!</i>

19:46.490 --> 19:48.290
Okay guys, this is where we begin!

19:49.130 --> 19:50.000
Yes!

19:50.000 --> 19:52.500
Damn you, Misugi.

19:52.500 --> 19:57.900
There wasn't any case that Misugi kept the ball himself and scored alone until now, right?

19:57.900 --> 20:01.510
Yeah. They scored with Misugi's assists in every game.

20:01.510 --> 20:06.880
<i>I thought he focused on passing to not strain his heart,</i>

20:06.880 --> 20:09.980
<i>but he's been well able to use his individual skills all along.</i>

20:09.980 --> 20:15.980
<i>That's the prodigy Jun Misugi for you.
But, we will have the first half end with this 3-1 score.</i>

20:15.980 --> 20:21.490
<i>Sawada, we will leave offense to Hyuga alone and focus on defense in first half.</i>

20:21.490 --> 20:22.990
<i>Got it!</i>

20:22.990 --> 20:24.080
<i>Damn you, Misugi.</i>

20:24.080 --> 20:25.220
<i>I will pay it back!</i>

20:25.220 --> 20:27.740
<i>I will score by myself this time.</i>

20:27.740 --> 20:30.150
<i>The match resumes with Toho's kick-off.</i>

20:31.230 --> 20:33.710
Scoring back when they score on me is my football!

20:33.710 --> 20:37.040
<i>Hyuga is kinda fired up with the first goal conceded.</i>

20:37.040 --> 20:38.180
<i>When this happens...</i>

20:38.180 --> 20:38.550
Come on!

20:38.550 --> 20:39.550
What?!

20:40.260 --> 20:44.050
<i>I will shake you nobodies off with my speed!</i>

20:44.050 --> 20:44.720
Now!

20:46.330 --> 20:49.370
<i>A precisely aimed team-play tackle from Misugi!</i>

20:50.020 --> 20:54.520
Football is not only about individual skills, team-play is also important, Hyuga.

20:54.520 --> 20:55.770
You little...!

20:55.770 --> 20:58.770
<i>Musashi advances up the pitch with quick passing!</i>

20:58.770 --> 21:02.030
<i>The game has entered Musashi's pace after Misugi got on!</i>

21:02.030 --> 21:08.200
<i>Toho has played perfectly up until now, yet they conceded a goal instantly.</i>

21:08.200 --> 21:10.700
<i>This mental shock is huge for them.</i>

21:11.110 --> 21:11.700
Honma!

21:12.580 --> 21:15.460
<i>Sawada cuts the cross aimed for Honma!</i>

21:15.460 --> 21:16.710
Okay, send it here, Takeshi!

21:18.710 --> 21:22.230
<i>Misugi reads Sawada's pass and cuts it!</i>

21:22.230 --> 21:24.130
<i>Misugi threatens to dribble here!</i>

21:27.020 --> 21:28.260
<i>No, he passed the ball!</i>

21:28.260 --> 21:30.510
<i>He makes an elegant one-two pass.</i>

21:30.510 --> 21:34.020
I got you, now the lead drops to one!

21:35.230 --> 21:37.980
Like I'd let you score again!

21:39.260 --> 21:40.560
<i>He caught it!</i>

21:40.560 --> 21:43.240
<i>Wakashimazu makes a brilliant jumping catch!</i>

21:45.530 --> 21:47.660
<i>That's Wakashimazu for you.</i>

21:47.660 --> 21:50.740
<i>Quick, explosive agility and jumping skill.</i>

21:50.740 --> 21:53.250
<i>It looks like I won't be able to score from long range.</i>

21:54.260 --> 21:56.000
<i>The first half ends here!</i>

21:56.000 --> 21:59.500
<i>The pace of the match started to flow in Musashi's favor when Misugi came on.</i>

21:59.500 --> 22:04.130
<i>But Toho has managed to fend off this counter attack and contain them to one goal.</i>

22:04.130 --> 22:06.350
<i>I won't let anyone get in my way.</i>

22:06.350 --> 22:11.350
<i>The one participating in the nationals and defeating Tsubasa will be me!</i>

22:11.350 --> 22:15.380
<i>I will not lose until I fight against Tsubasa again!</i>

22:38.790 --> 22:44.840
<i>chotto are mi na ace ga tooru</i>

22:38.790 --> 22:44.840
<i>Hey, look over there at the ace passing through</i>

22:44.840 --> 22:50.840
<i>suguremono zo to machijû sawagu</i>

22:44.840 --> 22:50.840
<i>He's the best, and the whole town cheers him on</i>

22:50.840 --> 22:56.890
<i>chô-chô samba, zigzag samba</i>

22:50.840 --> 22:56.890
<i>Butterfly samba, zig-zag samba</i>

22:56.890 --> 23:01.520
<i>aitsu no uwasa de chamba mo hashiru</i>

22:56.890 --> 23:01.520
<i>Even little old ladies go around talking about him</i>

23:03.150 --> 23:07.820
<i>sore ni tsukete mo ore-tacha nan na no</i>

23:03.150 --> 23:07.820
<i>So, even if we have him, who are we?</i>

23:09.150 --> 23:15.240
<i>ball hitotsu ni kiri-kiri mai sa</i>

23:09.150 --> 23:15.240
<i>The ball spins round and round</i>

23:15.240 --> 23:21.290
<i>Dash, dash, dash! Kick and dash!</i>

23:21.290 --> 23:25.750
<i>itsuka kimeru ze inazuma shoot</i>

23:21.290 --> 23:25.750
<i>One day, I'll score with a lightning shot!</i>

23:27.050 --> 23:33.390
<i>son toki ore ga super hero sa</i>

23:27.050 --> 23:33.390
<i>When that happens, I'll become a super hero!</i>

23:33.390 --> 23:39.430
<i>Dash, dash, dash! Kick and dash!</i>

23:39.430 --> 23:45.730
<i>moete seishun kakenukero</i>

23:39.430 --> 23:45.730
<i>This fierce youth is on the field!</i>

23:49.570 --> 24:03.170
COMING UP; EPISODE 33:
CONCLUSION OF TOKYO TOURNAMENT
